  "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference for HMW87 and HMW87D, pp. 76-85"
 },
 "notes": [
  "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
  "32-bit floats and 32-bit integers put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide's data-encoding section covers both formats and its worked read and write examples confirm the order.",
  "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
  "The guide's Modbus chapter applies only to HMW87 and HMW87D; the other HMDW80 models in the same guide are not covered by this map.",
  "Integer registers carry one decimal (raw x 0.1).",
  "Register 513 reads 0 when an error is active and 1 when there is none, as printed in the guide.",
  "Error codes 1024, 16384 and 32768 are readable only through Insight according to the guide, so they are not listed as status bits.",
  "Left out: display units register 3075, because the guide names the options (metric / non-metric) without giving their numeric values."
 ],
